# Mastermind document style

These files are **formal institutional policy and plans**, not technical manuals or chat notes.

## Rules

- Formal Thai policy register: complete sentences, numbered sections (๑ ๒ ๓), dignified diction
- Clear and concise — decide direction without casual asides, arrows, or slogan tone
- One concern per file; no implementation steps, command lists, or schema dumps
- Prefer short tables and numbered principles over long prose
- Update only when direction changes — not on every code change
- Link to `docs/` for technical truth; do not copy it here
- Distill source material into policy points; do not make channels or source files into section topics
- Keep terms stable: SACRED, Mahāpadesa, Identity, Corpus, Alignment, Service; user groups ก/ข/ค

## Do not

- Write in informal bullet shorthand or conversational Thai
- Elevate website/homepage/comms sync into a policy heading
- Add status inventories of the repo
- Add AI/feature brainstorms that skip Identity → Corpus → Alignment → Service
- Inflate files past what a decision-maker needs in one sitting
